Subject: [PATCH] linux-atm: fix six genuine defects exposed by gcc warnings

These are behaviour bugs, not style noise. Each was confirmed by reading the
source, not inferred from the diagnostic alone.

sapequal.c - CHECK(FIELD, CONSTRAINT) pasted CONSTRAINT unparenthesized into
  `!CONSTRAINT`, so CHECK(l3.itu.window, a.x > b.x) expanded to
  `(!a.x) > b.x`. The SSCOP/BLLI negotiation constraint was therefore never
  evaluated as written. Add the missing parentheses in the macro.

ans.c - `if (addr->sas_addr.prv)` tests the address of an array member
  (unsigned char prv[ATM_ESA_LEN], kernel linux/atm.h:209), which is never
  NULL, so the E.164 else branch was dead code. The rest of the library tests
  the first byte: atm2text.c:89, atmequal.c:37, text2atm.c:132. Do the same.

asn_bits.c - AsnBitsEquiv compared b1->bits[octetsLessOne] against itself, so
  two BIT STRINGs differing only in the significant bits of the final octet
  compared equal. The right hand side must be b2.

mib.c - `result` is only assigned inside `while (var->name != NULL)`. For an
  empty MIB table the loop body never runs and result is read uninitialized.
  Initialize it to AsnOidLess (first enumerator, util.h:38), which routes an
  empty table to the existing "object not found" branch.

mpoad/io.c - complete_connection() passes an uninitialized sockaddr_atmsvc to
  connect(); the syscall copies sizeof(dummy) bytes from userspace before the
  protocol handler runs. The call only exists to read back errno, so zero the
  address first.

proto.c - free_call() printed the pointer after free(). Passing the value to
  %p does not dereference it, but it is still a use of an indeterminate
  pointer; print before freeing.

--- a/src/ilmid/asn1/asn_bits.c
+++ b/src/ilmid/asn1/asn_bits.c
@@ -346,7 +346,7 @@
     return ( (b1->bitLen == b2->bitLen) &&
              (memcmp(b1->bits, b2->bits, octetsLessOne) == 0) &&
              (( b1->bits[octetsLessOne] & (0xFF << octetBits)) ==
-              ( b1->bits[octetsLessOne] & (0xFF << octetBits))));
+              ( b2->bits[octetsLessOne] & (0xFF << octetBits))));
 
 } /* AsnBitsEquiv */
 
--- a/src/ilmid/mib.c
+++ b/src/ilmid/mib.c
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@
 {
   VarBind *varbind;
   Variable *var;
-  AsnOidResult result;
+  AsnOidResult result = AsnOidLess;
   
   *offset = 1;
   FOR_EACH_LIST_ELMT(varbind, list)
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@
 {
   VarBind *varbind;
   Variable *var;
-  AsnOidResult result;
+  AsnOidResult result = AsnOidLess;
 
   *offset = 1;
   FOR_EACH_LIST_ELMT(varbind, list)
